From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_balloon: finer free-page reporting and harder
 free-page hinting

Two reporting-path improvements so idle/fragmented memory reaches the
host instead of stranding in the guest:

- Page reporting order: the default (pageblock_order, 4MB on 4K) only
  reports fully-coalesced pageblocks, so fragmented free memory that can't
  coalesce is never reported. On 4K-page kernels report order-9 (2MB)
  blocks instead, like the existing ARM64/64K special-case reports 2MB.
  The reporting core scans that order upward, so both 2MB and 4MB free
  chunks are reported. 2MB also matches the host THP size, avoiding THP
  splits. Still overridable at boot via
  page_reporting.page_reporting_order=.
- Free-page-hint allocation: VIRTIO_BALLOON_FREE_PAGE_ALLOC_FLAG loses
  __GFP_NORETRY in favour of __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL (same treatment as
  balloon_page_alloc), so 4MB hint blocks survive pressure via reclaim
  instead of failing fast, while still failing rather than OOM-killing.

Only active when the host negotiates F_REPORTING / F_FREE_PAGE_HINT
(Firecracker: free_page_reporting / free_page_hinting device options).

Signed-off-by: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
---
 drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
index 123456789016..123456789021 100644
--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
@@ -31,7 +31,12 @@
 #define VIRTIO_BALLOON_OOM_NR_PAGES 1024
 #define VIRTIO_BALLOON_OOM_NOTIFY_PRIORITY 80

-#define VIRTIO_BALLOON_FREE_PAGE_ALLOC_FLAG (__GFP_NORETRY | __GFP_NOWARN | \
+/*
+ * Aggressive: allow reclaim for free-page-hint blocks too, so 4MB hint
+ * blocks survive pressure instead of failing fast. Still fails (rather
+ * than OOM-killing) when nothing is reclaimable.
+ */
+#define VIRTIO_BALLOON_FREE_PAGE_ALLOC_FLAG (__GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL | __GFP_NOWARN | \
 					     __GFP_NOMEMALLOC)
 /* The order of free page blocks to report to host */
 #define VIRTIO_BALLOON_HINT_BLOCK_ORDER MAX_PAGE_ORDER
@@ -1073,6 +1078,15 @@
 		 */
 #if defined(CONFIG_ARM64) && defined(CONFIG_ARM64_64K_PAGES)
 		vb->pr_dev_info.order = 5;
+#elif PAGE_SHIFT == 12
+		/*
+		 * Aggressive: report 2MB blocks instead of the default
+		 * pageblock-sized ones, so fragmented free memory that can't
+		 * coalesce into a full pageblock is still reported to the
+		 * host. 2MB also matches the host THP size, avoiding splits.
+		 * (Overridable at boot via page_reporting.page_reporting_order.)
+		 */
+		vb->pr_dev_info.order = 9;
 #endif

 		err = page_reporting_register(&vb->pr_dev_info);

--
2.47.0
